WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.295 --> 00:00:04.128
- Hello, Believe Nation!

00:00:04.128 --> 00:00:05.456
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:05.456 --> 00:00:08.018
My one word is believe, and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:08.018 --> 00:00:10.797
will solve all of the
world's major problems,

00:00:10.797 --> 00:00:12.109
so to help you on your journey today,

00:00:12.109 --> 00:00:13.823
I'm going to talk about seven ways

00:00:13.823 --> 00:00:15.945
to improve your people skills.

00:00:15.945 --> 00:00:18.862
(electronic music)

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:25.564
So, I often get asked, from entrepreneurs,

00:00:25.564 --> 00:00:27.015
how do I improve my people skills?

00:00:27.015 --> 00:00:29.495
Evan, I need help,
either with my customers,

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:30.597
either when I'm marketing,

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:33.028
and going out to trade
shows, or I'm meeting people,

00:00:33.028 --> 00:00:35.052
or I'm with my team, how
to be a better leader.

00:00:35.052 --> 00:00:36.726
How do I improve my people skills?

00:00:36.726 --> 00:00:37.784
And so, I thought I'd make this video,

00:00:37.784 --> 00:00:40.194
sharing seven different
ways I think will help you

00:00:40.194 --> 00:00:41.694
in your challenge.

00:00:44.621 --> 00:00:47.152
So, tip number one, is decide
what you want to improve.

00:00:47.152 --> 00:00:49.829
There's a lot of different
things around people skills,

00:00:49.829 --> 00:00:52.164
and if you want to improve at all of them,

00:00:52.164 --> 00:00:54.708
it can be a challenge, and
you may not even want to.

00:00:54.708 --> 00:00:57.122
So, having focus gives you clarity,

00:00:57.122 --> 00:01:00.236
and allows you to really improve.

00:01:00.236 --> 00:01:01.618
So, as an example, do you want to improve

00:01:01.618 --> 00:01:02.479
your networking skills?

00:01:02.479 --> 00:01:03.963
Do you want to improve
your leadership skills?

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:06.692
Do you want to improve
your social setting skills?

00:01:06.692 --> 00:01:08.807
You know, what is it exactly
that you want to improve,

00:01:08.807 --> 00:01:10.299
and we can figure that out.

00:01:10.299 --> 00:01:12.575
And just focus on the
one most important thing,

00:01:12.575 --> 00:01:14.369
like maybe you really want
to be a better leader,

00:01:14.369 --> 00:01:16.539
but you don't really care that
much about the networking,

00:01:16.539 --> 00:01:17.771
or maybe you don't even have a team yet.

00:01:17.771 --> 00:01:19.483
You don't care about leadership skills.

00:01:19.483 --> 00:01:21.084
Maybe, all you want to
do, is get more sales,

00:01:21.084 --> 00:01:22.171
and you're going to events,

00:01:22.171 --> 00:01:23.749
and you want to learn how to shake hands,

00:01:23.749 --> 00:01:26.011
and make a connection
really quick with people.

00:01:26.011 --> 00:01:29.027
Figure out exactly what it
is that you want to learn.

00:01:29.027 --> 00:01:30.813
If you can get that focus and clarity,

00:01:30.813 --> 00:01:32.852
it's much more easier
to make rapid progress,

00:01:32.852 --> 00:01:34.519
achieving your goal.

00:01:37.553 --> 00:01:39.356
Step number two, is model success.

00:01:39.356 --> 00:01:40.766
And this is always a go-to for me.

00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:42.090
If you don't know what you're doing,

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.104
if you're trying to learn something,

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.340
one of the fastest ways to do it,

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.986
is find someone who's already
done it, and learn from them.

00:01:47.986 --> 00:01:51.132
Instead of you struggling,
and trying to figure it out,

00:01:51.132 --> 00:01:53.520
learn from someone's who's
already gone out and done it.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.392
It'll massively shortcut
your path to success,

00:01:56.392 --> 00:01:57.805
and you may not even figure it out

00:01:57.805 --> 00:01:59.084
most of the things that you're trying,

00:01:59.084 --> 00:02:01.264
until you get that
input from someone else.

00:02:01.264 --> 00:02:03.509
And so, again, having the clarity,

00:02:03.509 --> 00:02:06.001
I want to be a master networker, great.

00:02:06.001 --> 00:02:08.885
Who is a master networker in your eyes?

00:02:08.885 --> 00:02:10.737
Go to YouTube, look at different videos.

00:02:10.737 --> 00:02:13.445
You can read different books,
you can attend conferences.

00:02:13.445 --> 00:02:14.701
Find the master networker!

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.678
Or, I don't care about networking,
I care about leadership!

00:02:16.678 --> 00:02:19.023
Great, who are the leadership experts?

00:02:19.023 --> 00:02:20.099
How can I hang around them?

00:02:20.099 --> 00:02:21.866
How can I be with them,
as much as possible?

00:02:21.866 --> 00:02:23.963
Going to their events,
reading their books,

00:02:23.963 --> 00:02:26.113
being around them, watching their videos?

00:02:26.113 --> 00:02:27.238
And I would highly encourage you

00:02:27.238 --> 00:02:31.876
not just to read content, not
just to look at the how-tos,

00:02:31.876 --> 00:02:32.897
because everybody will have,

00:02:32.897 --> 00:02:35.084
here are the seven ways to do it!

00:02:35.084 --> 00:02:37.163
Rhetorically, will have their list.

00:02:37.163 --> 00:02:41.456
But, to feel it, to see
how they do it, right?

00:02:41.456 --> 00:02:45.769
So, if I'm making a video about
how to write a book, right?

00:02:45.769 --> 00:02:47.832
Don't just watch the video
about how to write the book,

00:02:47.832 --> 00:02:49.989
watch me document the process.

00:02:49.989 --> 00:02:51.708
I mean, I don't know how many videos.

00:02:51.708 --> 00:02:54.741
I made over 50 videos,
documenting the process.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:55.574
Watch that,

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:57.733
or watch somebody else
going through the process.

00:02:57.733 --> 00:03:01.147
Having the how-to videos is
great, it's a starting point,

00:03:01.147 --> 00:03:04.005
but a lot of the content
is also going to come,

00:03:04.005 --> 00:03:05.896
by just watching them.

00:03:05.896 --> 00:03:08.150
So, just reading an article about

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:10.981
how to make an introduction to somebody,

00:03:10.981 --> 00:03:14.111
versus watching somebody, who's
really good at it, doing it,

00:03:14.111 --> 00:03:15.801
and demoing it, and showing it,

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:17.540
and guiding other people through it,

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.413
you'll learn a lot more
through that process,

00:03:19.413 --> 00:03:21.035
than just by reading an article.

00:03:21.035 --> 00:03:23.337
And so, when you clearly
identify, back to step one,

00:03:23.337 --> 00:03:25.572
clearly identify what it is
that you want to work on,

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:26.687
then go off of model success,

00:03:26.687 --> 00:03:28.782
find a person who's the genius at it,

00:03:28.782 --> 00:03:30.719
and try to be around them.

00:03:30.719 --> 00:03:34.526
Go to their event, see them do
it live, watch their videos,

00:03:34.526 --> 00:03:36.724
and get their books,
and read their content,

00:03:36.724 --> 00:03:38.312
but I want you to see it, and feel it,

00:03:38.312 --> 00:03:40.290
'cause when you can feel
it on an emotional level,

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:43.176
and not just understand it, up here,

00:03:43.176 --> 00:03:47.343
you're much more likely to
retain it, and take action.

00:03:49.418 --> 00:03:52.173
Tip number three, practice,
practice, practice,

00:03:52.173 --> 00:03:53.072
like anything else!

00:03:53.072 --> 00:03:55.000
You want to get better at
somethin', you got to practice!

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.004
You got to dedicate time to
it, consistently, every day,

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.768
to practice, to get better, to improve.

00:03:59.768 --> 00:04:02.082
So, we've identified what
it is about people skills

00:04:02.082 --> 00:04:03.294
we want to work on.

00:04:03.294 --> 00:04:04.229
We've modeled success,

00:04:04.229 --> 00:04:05.723
and found the best people in the world

00:04:05.723 --> 00:04:06.556
that are doin' it.

00:04:06.556 --> 00:04:07.389
We've attended some of their events,

00:04:07.389 --> 00:04:09.672
we've watched their videos,
we've read their books,

00:04:09.672 --> 00:04:10.976
great, that's just knowledge!

00:04:10.976 --> 00:04:12.043
It's not going to actually happen

00:04:12.043 --> 00:04:13.659
'til you do somethin' about it.

00:04:13.659 --> 00:04:17.735
You can understand how do to
do a jump, on a snowboard,

00:04:17.735 --> 00:04:19.223
but you're not going to
get the muscle memory

00:04:19.223 --> 00:04:21.428
and actually be able to
perform it, until you practice,

00:04:21.428 --> 00:04:23.372
and you're going to fall,
and fall, and fall, and fall,

00:04:23.372 --> 00:04:24.258
and get better and practice.

00:04:24.258 --> 00:04:26.446
And so, whatever it is
that you improve on,

00:04:26.446 --> 00:04:27.461
you got to put in the reps.

00:04:27.461 --> 00:04:30.094
I've made 5,000 videos, on
this YouTube channel, right?

00:04:30.094 --> 00:04:32.611
1,000 of them are not even public.

00:04:32.611 --> 00:04:35.735
Though, 1,000 videos, which
is more than most people do,

00:04:35.735 --> 00:04:39.703
in general, on a YouTube channel,
that are not even public.

00:04:39.703 --> 00:04:41.502
I've just brought Lily
on board, on my team,

00:04:41.502 --> 00:04:44.836
if you've watched Unlocking
Lily series, and right now,

00:04:44.836 --> 00:04:46.225
I'm filling up her schedule.

00:04:46.225 --> 00:04:49.270
When she does an Unlocking Lily video,

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:52.374
her first video, it took
over 100 takes, each time,

00:04:52.374 --> 00:04:53.857
to get that best version.

00:04:53.857 --> 00:04:57.165
And she'll spend every
Friday, the whole day,

00:04:57.165 --> 00:04:59.156
filming, filming,
filming, filming, filming,

00:04:59.156 --> 00:05:00.691
hundreds of takes.

00:05:00.691 --> 00:05:02.176
And if you've watched her first video,

00:05:02.176 --> 00:05:03.309
she only got three videos.

00:05:03.309 --> 00:05:05.723
Her first, to the second, to the third,

00:05:05.723 --> 00:05:08.225
you'll see that she's gotten
way better in each one,

00:05:08.225 --> 00:05:09.800
but she's put in the work.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:11.023
And so, I'm filling up her schedule.

00:05:11.023 --> 00:05:13.454
I'm giving her interviews, I'm
giving her coaching sessions.

00:05:13.454 --> 00:05:15.235
I'm giving her entrepreneurs to talk to.

00:05:15.235 --> 00:05:17.417
I'm giving her opportunities to speak,

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:19.310
opportunities to be in the video.

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:21.980
Her schedule is just rammed, full, right?

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:24.748
She came here, and she did
two videos with me, today,

00:05:24.748 --> 00:05:27.940
filming day, and she just came
back from a coaching calling

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:29.264
interview, then she had to rush back,

00:05:29.264 --> 00:05:31.201
to do more coaching
calls, more interviews,

00:05:31.201 --> 00:05:32.437
the whole day is full,

00:05:32.437 --> 00:05:33.693
because she's puttin' in the reps!

00:05:33.693 --> 00:05:35.782
'Cause, she's really good now,

00:05:35.782 --> 00:05:38.365
but to get great, to get
to where she wants to be,

00:05:38.365 --> 00:05:39.966
to build a million dollar business

00:05:39.966 --> 00:05:42.285
around speaking and coaching,
that she wants to do,

00:05:42.285 --> 00:05:43.443
that I'm here to help her with,

00:05:43.443 --> 00:05:45.980
she's got to put in
repetitions, to get better.

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:48.499
And so, practice, whatever you learn,

00:05:48.499 --> 00:05:50.886
whatever that thing is, that
you pull from that expert,

00:05:50.886 --> 00:05:52.947
that you want to learn, you
got to put in the practice,

00:05:52.947 --> 00:05:55.664
and find somebody to work.

00:05:55.664 --> 00:05:58.456
So, if it's networking, great,
you've learned the skill,

00:05:58.456 --> 00:05:59.677
now go out and practice!

00:05:59.677 --> 00:06:01.749
Going to one networking event a month

00:06:01.749 --> 00:06:02.807
is not going to do it!

00:06:02.807 --> 00:06:05.764
You got to, multiple events, per week.

00:06:05.764 --> 00:06:07.561
Practice networking on the subway.

00:06:07.561 --> 00:06:10.328
Like everyday, you want to
hone your skills of practice.

00:06:10.328 --> 00:06:12.058
If it's about rapport building,

00:06:12.058 --> 00:06:14.576
maybe you learn about
how to match and mirror,

00:06:14.576 --> 00:06:17.249
and so, you're learning
matching body language, right?

00:06:17.249 --> 00:06:19.593
If somebody's goin' like this,
you kind of go like this.

00:06:19.593 --> 00:06:21.301
If somebody's arms crossed,

00:06:21.301 --> 00:06:22.705
then you start with your arms crossed,

00:06:22.705 --> 00:06:23.611
and you try to lead them,

00:06:23.611 --> 00:06:25.409
to get them to have their arms open.

00:06:25.409 --> 00:06:27.609
It's when you know you've
established some rapport.

00:06:27.609 --> 00:06:28.442
Matching and mirroring.

00:06:28.442 --> 00:06:29.533
Great, practice that!

00:06:29.533 --> 00:06:30.882
Practice it with your family,

00:06:30.882 --> 00:06:33.683
practice it with your friends,
even without telling 'em!

00:06:33.683 --> 00:06:34.855
You're just practicing!

00:06:34.855 --> 00:06:36.065
And sometimes, you're going to fail,

00:06:36.065 --> 00:06:36.898
especially at the beginning.

00:06:36.898 --> 00:06:37.731
You will suck.

00:06:37.731 --> 00:06:38.840
A lot of these methods won't work

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:40.430
quite as you expect them to,

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:42.167
because you're just
starting out, and you suck.

00:06:42.167 --> 00:06:43.360
Expect that to happen.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:45.882
How you get better, is you
practice, practice, practice,

00:06:45.882 --> 00:06:46.715
practice, practice.

00:06:46.715 --> 00:06:48.269
'Cause, you have the knowledge.

00:06:48.269 --> 00:06:49.946
You know what you're supposed to do,

00:06:49.946 --> 00:06:52.004
but you can't actually do it yet.

00:06:52.004 --> 00:06:54.916
You get it, by putting the
work, doing the practice,

00:06:54.916 --> 00:06:56.749
and building a muscle.

00:06:59.503 --> 00:07:01.212
- We got it, we're in?

00:07:01.212 --> 00:07:02.045
Awesome.

00:07:02.045 --> 00:07:05.261
Misfit Nation has just
taken over Seven Ways.

00:07:05.261 --> 00:07:07.019
Hi, everyone, my name is Dave Lukas.

00:07:07.019 --> 00:07:10.014
I'm the host of the Misfit
Entrepreneur podcast,

00:07:10.014 --> 00:07:11.900
and we are tackling number four,

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:14.177
in Seven Ways, in people skills this week.

00:07:14.177 --> 00:07:17.082
The answer I have for you is
actually a two-part answer,

00:07:17.082 --> 00:07:18.922
and the first part is actually something

00:07:18.922 --> 00:07:20.975
that I learned from a mentor of mine,

00:07:20.975 --> 00:07:22.570
that ran a Fortune 100 company,

00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:24.350
and I learned it many years ago.

00:07:24.350 --> 00:07:25.931
And it goes like this.

00:07:25.931 --> 00:07:27.953
If you want to know what John Smith buys,

00:07:27.953 --> 00:07:30.481
you have to see things
through John Smith's eyes.

00:07:30.481 --> 00:07:32.225
And what that means, is
that you really need to

00:07:32.225 --> 00:07:34.455
put yourself in the other person's shoes.

00:07:34.455 --> 00:07:36.858
You really need to understand
what motivates them,

00:07:36.858 --> 00:07:38.457
what drives them, what they care about,

00:07:38.457 --> 00:07:42.481
what the levers are, that
really drive their decisions,

00:07:42.481 --> 00:07:44.271
and why they do things.

00:07:44.271 --> 00:07:45.737
Once you understand that,

00:07:45.737 --> 00:07:47.686
and understand what they
want out of something,

00:07:47.686 --> 00:07:49.494
then it makes it that much easier,

00:07:49.494 --> 00:07:53.227
to get what you want, or
be able to get the outcome

00:07:53.227 --> 00:07:54.060
that you're looking for,

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:55.599
whether you're negotiating a deal,

00:07:55.599 --> 00:07:56.890
putting together a big project,

00:07:56.890 --> 00:07:58.970
or just want to work better with somebody.

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:00.019
The second part of this,

00:08:00.019 --> 00:08:02.474
there's actually a concept
made famous by Zig Ziglar,

00:08:02.474 --> 00:08:04.468
and that goes like this,

00:08:04.468 --> 00:08:06.277
if you help somebody get what they want,

00:08:06.277 --> 00:08:07.891
you'll get what you want, and more,

00:08:07.891 --> 00:08:10.518
and really, it's the law of reciprocity.

00:08:10.518 --> 00:08:13.017
So, the more that you are
focused on helping others

00:08:13.017 --> 00:08:15.503
get what they want, and
accomplish the things they want,

00:08:15.503 --> 00:08:16.922
you'll be amazed at what it does for you.

00:08:16.922 --> 00:08:18.517
It'll come back to you tenfold.

00:08:18.517 --> 00:08:20.224
So, when you pair those two together,

00:08:20.224 --> 00:08:23.741
really understanding what
drives someone, motivates them,

00:08:23.741 --> 00:08:26.770
and then looking for the best
way to help them get there,

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:30.500
and make it mutually
beneficial, everybody wins,

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:31.891
and that's the important thing.

00:08:31.891 --> 00:08:34.993
So, that's number four,
in Seven Ways, this week.

00:08:34.993 --> 00:08:35.900
Hopefully, you can take that,

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:37.300
and put it to work in your life right now,

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:38.731
and make a big difference.

00:08:38.731 --> 00:08:39.564
Thank you.

00:08:43.062 --> 00:08:45.449
- Tip number five is find
something you're curious about.

00:08:45.449 --> 00:08:47.851
The easiest conversation
to have with somebody,

00:08:47.851 --> 00:08:49.521
the easiest way to connect
with somebody else,

00:08:49.521 --> 00:08:52.958
is through some kind of joint love.

00:08:52.958 --> 00:08:54.047
So, if you can find somethin'

00:08:54.047 --> 00:08:56.440
that you are genuinely curious about,

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:59.185
then it's way easier
to have a conversation.

00:08:59.185 --> 00:09:00.712
It's way easier to get to know them.

00:09:00.712 --> 00:09:03.583
So, for example, for me,
anything around entrepreneurship,

00:09:03.583 --> 00:09:06.652
I am generally going
to love to talk to you.

00:09:06.652 --> 00:09:08.026
If I find out that you're an entrepreneur,

00:09:08.026 --> 00:09:09.957
we are going to have
an amazing discussion.

00:09:09.957 --> 00:09:10.910
It's just going to happen.

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:14.783
You will, immediately,
perk up my excitement,

00:09:14.783 --> 00:09:16.882
and I'm going to want to
challenge you, talk to you,

00:09:16.882 --> 00:09:18.746
understand you, see how I can help you,

00:09:18.746 --> 00:09:20.289
Even if we only have
five minutes together,

00:09:20.289 --> 00:09:22.057
I want to be able to provide value,

00:09:22.057 --> 00:09:23.417
and get you on your path.

00:09:23.417 --> 00:09:25.000
It's just who I am.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.184
And so, try to find some
kind of common ground,

00:09:27.184 --> 00:09:28.747
between you and the other person.

00:09:28.747 --> 00:09:29.653
It'll really help.

00:09:29.653 --> 00:09:31.496
Now, you could do, if you know in advance,

00:09:31.496 --> 00:09:32.846
anything about that person,

00:09:32.846 --> 00:09:35.559
you can stalk them on Twitter,
and Instagram, and Facebook,

00:09:35.559 --> 00:09:38.144
and YouTube, and just kind
of understand a little bit

00:09:38.144 --> 00:09:39.962
about them, what they
may be interested in,

00:09:39.962 --> 00:09:41.291
and you don't want to lead with,

00:09:41.291 --> 00:09:44.538
hey, I saw that you loved
horseshoes, on Twitter!

00:09:44.538 --> 00:09:45.371
That's awesome!

00:09:45.371 --> 00:09:46.290
Tell me about horseshoes!

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:48.469
'Cause, if you don't actually
care about horseshoes,

00:09:48.469 --> 00:09:49.468
then it's a disconnect,

00:09:49.468 --> 00:09:51.672
and it's kind of creepy stalker scary,

00:09:51.672 --> 00:09:52.970
so you don't want to let them know

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:55.053
that you've been following
them along on Twitter.

00:09:55.053 --> 00:09:57.700
But, if you find something
that's generally interesting,

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:58.982
that's the key.

00:09:58.982 --> 00:09:59.815
And so, you can start,

00:09:59.815 --> 00:10:00.898
if you don't know anything about them,

00:10:00.898 --> 00:10:02.496
you could start an event.

00:10:02.496 --> 00:10:03.549
Well, how did they come to this event?

00:10:03.549 --> 00:10:04.853
You're both at this event.

00:10:04.853 --> 00:10:06.376
What motivated them to come here?

00:10:06.376 --> 00:10:07.329
How do they know the host?

00:10:07.329 --> 00:10:08.380
How did they find this place?

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:09.880
Did they search for it online?

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:11.672
What were their reasons for coming here?

00:10:11.672 --> 00:10:13.366
That opens up a discussion,

00:10:13.366 --> 00:10:16.220
and then, you're looking for
ways to generally be curious

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:17.614
about the other person.

00:10:17.614 --> 00:10:20.379
If you can find any kind of
genuine connection there,

00:10:20.379 --> 00:10:22.389
then it's easy to get them
to talk about themselves,

00:10:22.389 --> 00:10:25.306
and it's easy to form that rapport.

00:10:27.718 --> 00:10:29.944
Tip number six, is understand their why.

00:10:29.944 --> 00:10:31.586
People love talking about themselves,

00:10:31.586 --> 00:10:33.988
and I love getting people excited.

00:10:33.988 --> 00:10:35.419
So, when I'm talking to entrepreneurs,

00:10:35.419 --> 00:10:38.163
I like understanding why
they started their business.

00:10:38.163 --> 00:10:40.136
Because, I want to get them pumped up.

00:10:40.136 --> 00:10:41.533
If you are talking about something

00:10:41.533 --> 00:10:43.339
that is meaningful to you,

00:10:43.339 --> 00:10:44.991
that on a deep, emotional level,

00:10:44.991 --> 00:10:49.065
it gets you feeling excited,
like this is your purpose,

00:10:49.065 --> 00:10:51.526
then it's so much easier to follow through

00:10:51.526 --> 00:10:52.380
on a conversation.

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:53.423
If I'm talking to an entrepreneur,

00:10:53.423 --> 00:10:54.835
I ask them, why they
started their business.

00:10:54.835 --> 00:10:55.986
And they tell me this story,

00:10:55.986 --> 00:10:58.218
about this deep, meaningful connection,

00:10:58.218 --> 00:10:59.409
to this product they're making,

00:10:59.409 --> 00:11:00.408
or service they're making,

00:11:00.408 --> 00:11:01.787
and they started because of their parents,

00:11:01.787 --> 00:11:03.687
or whatever that backstory is.

00:11:03.687 --> 00:11:06.086
There has to be something there

00:11:06.086 --> 00:11:09.114
that fueled them to want to do this thing.

00:11:09.114 --> 00:11:10.454
And whether it shows up to this event,

00:11:10.454 --> 00:11:13.127
or choose that career
path, or marry that person.

00:11:13.127 --> 00:11:15.835
Whatever it is, if you
understand their why,

00:11:15.835 --> 00:11:17.371
and get them excited about it,

00:11:17.371 --> 00:11:20.053
it's much more easy to form
a bond, and a connection.

00:11:20.053 --> 00:11:22.545
When people ask me my why,

00:11:22.545 --> 00:11:23.730
and they genuinely care about it.

00:11:23.730 --> 00:11:25.680
If you have to actually
care, you can't just fake,

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:28.109
and say, so, why did you do this?

00:11:28.109 --> 00:11:31.256
With genuine curiosity,
why do you do this thing?

00:11:31.256 --> 00:11:32.339
It's awesome.

00:11:33.345 --> 00:11:36.164
You'll get, if you ask me,
that you get me being excited,

00:11:36.164 --> 00:11:39.466
if you get me telling an
excited story, like I am now,

00:11:39.466 --> 00:11:40.943
then I'm much more likely
to connect with you,

00:11:40.943 --> 00:11:42.558
and much more likely to want
to do business with you,

00:11:42.558 --> 00:11:43.714
much more likely to want to refer you,

00:11:43.714 --> 00:11:45.284
and much more likely to
take whatever action it is

00:11:45.284 --> 00:11:46.527
that you want me to take,

00:11:46.527 --> 00:11:48.501
even if it's just get to know each other,

00:11:48.501 --> 00:11:50.595
exchange contact information.

00:11:50.595 --> 00:11:52.569
Whatever it is, if you can get somebody

00:11:52.569 --> 00:11:54.884
to explain their why,
on an emotional level,

00:11:54.884 --> 00:11:56.668
because you generally care about it,

00:11:56.668 --> 00:12:00.335
then it's much more
easy to build a rapport.

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:04.971
And tip number seven, is
help them with their goals,

00:12:04.971 --> 00:12:06.383
and this builds off of what Dave,

00:12:06.383 --> 00:12:08.341
from Misfit Entrepreneur, was saying.

00:12:08.341 --> 00:12:09.978
You want to try to help
them accomplish what it is

00:12:09.978 --> 00:12:11.185
that they're trying to accomplish.

00:12:11.185 --> 00:12:12.731
I'd like to say, internally in my team,

00:12:12.731 --> 00:12:14.656
that the most dangerous
thing that you can do,

00:12:14.656 --> 00:12:15.996
is tell me what your goal is.

00:12:15.996 --> 00:12:17.408
'Cause, as soon as I
know what your goal is,

00:12:17.408 --> 00:12:19.439
what your dream is, now it's on my radar,

00:12:19.439 --> 00:12:21.090
and I'm going to try to
make it happen for you,

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:23.511
and I'm going to push
you, to go off and do it.

00:12:23.511 --> 00:12:25.045
And when you say, that you can't do it,

00:12:25.045 --> 00:12:27.465
because of XYZ, and whatever
limiting beliefs you have,

00:12:27.465 --> 00:12:29.004
we're pushing through those things, baby!

00:12:29.004 --> 00:12:30.195
It's going to happen.

00:12:30.195 --> 00:12:33.767
And so, I try to do that
with everybody I meet.

00:12:33.767 --> 00:12:35.365
It's not even a strategy,
it's just natural.

00:12:35.365 --> 00:12:36.608
Just what I try to do.

00:12:36.608 --> 00:12:37.768
I don't even think about it,

00:12:37.768 --> 00:12:39.446
but now that we're kind of making a list

00:12:39.446 --> 00:12:40.864
of seven things to do,

00:12:40.864 --> 00:12:43.577
it's one I think can be highly,
highly, highly effective.

00:12:43.577 --> 00:12:45.467
When I went to ClamourCon recently,

00:12:45.467 --> 00:12:47.336
it was an event for YouTubers,

00:12:47.336 --> 00:12:49.201
one of my main things was
every time I met somebody,

00:12:49.201 --> 00:12:51.263
I tried to introduce them to somebody else

00:12:51.263 --> 00:12:52.123
that could help.

00:12:52.123 --> 00:12:53.976
So, there was Sean,
from Video Influencers,

00:12:53.976 --> 00:12:56.120
who was tryin' to interview YouTubers.

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:57.926
And I asked him, how many he had set up?

00:12:57.926 --> 00:12:58.794
Like, what's your goal?

00:12:58.794 --> 00:12:59.627
What are you tryin' to accomplish?

00:12:59.627 --> 00:13:00.715
How many people are
you tryin' to interview

00:13:00.715 --> 00:13:01.548
while you're here?

00:13:01.548 --> 00:13:02.381
And he had this target.

00:13:02.381 --> 00:13:03.537
Like, how many have you done so far?

00:13:03.537 --> 00:13:04.482
And then, he's here.

00:13:04.482 --> 00:13:06.764
Great, if I find somebody that's relevant,

00:13:06.764 --> 00:13:07.793
do you want me to introduce you?

00:13:07.793 --> 00:13:09.272
"Yes, that'd be amazing!"

00:13:09.272 --> 00:13:10.105
Awesome!

00:13:10.105 --> 00:13:11.223
So, every time I met an entrepreneur,

00:13:11.223 --> 00:13:13.344
a YouTuber who had certain channel size,

00:13:13.344 --> 00:13:15.251
I thought might be a
fit for Sean's channel,

00:13:15.251 --> 00:13:17.729
I've watched Sean's videos,
so I know what it's all about,

00:13:17.729 --> 00:13:18.724
I would introduce them.

00:13:18.724 --> 00:13:21.148
And Sean is happy, and the
other entrepreneur is happy,

00:13:21.148 --> 00:13:22.534
'cause they're getting exposure.

00:13:22.534 --> 00:13:25.102
And I'm happy that I was
able to make that connection.

00:13:25.102 --> 00:13:27.929
It was to the point, where
Charlie, from Chris on Command,

00:13:27.929 --> 00:13:29.748
one of the channels that I love watching,

00:13:29.748 --> 00:13:30.928
I met him at ClamourCon.

00:13:30.928 --> 00:13:32.213
I introduced him to Sean.

00:13:32.213 --> 00:13:34.556
He's going to be a guest,
on Video Influencers.

00:13:34.556 --> 00:13:35.742
Charlie, then, went to his channel.

00:13:35.742 --> 00:13:39.868
He made a video about how
to network, as an introvert,

00:13:39.868 --> 00:13:40.701
which was me,

00:13:40.701 --> 00:13:41.608
and the video's basically about me,

00:13:41.608 --> 00:13:43.746
and my strategies at ClamourCon,

00:13:43.746 --> 00:13:45.695
and how amazed he was
at all the connections

00:13:45.695 --> 00:13:46.555
that I was able to make,

00:13:46.555 --> 00:13:49.011
despite not really
knowing a lot of people.

00:13:49.011 --> 00:13:50.284
And a lot of us, just based on this,

00:13:50.284 --> 00:13:52.471
it's not that I'm some genius,

00:13:52.471 --> 00:13:55.269
it's just I meet somebody,
I understand their why,

00:13:55.269 --> 00:13:56.571
I ask questions about them.

00:13:56.571 --> 00:13:58.423
I try to figure what their goal is,

00:13:58.423 --> 00:14:01.804
not from a strategic point of
view, it's just how I think.

00:14:01.804 --> 00:14:03.719
And then, I just keep that in my head.

00:14:03.719 --> 00:14:05.067
This person is trying to accomplish this.

00:14:05.067 --> 00:14:07.147
I meet somebody else,
and huh, you guys might,

00:14:07.147 --> 00:14:08.351
do you know Charlie?

00:14:08.351 --> 00:14:09.184
Do you know Sean?

00:14:09.184 --> 00:14:10.309
Do you know this guy?

00:14:10.309 --> 00:14:12.277
I just try to make those
natural connections.

00:14:12.277 --> 00:14:14.211
It's just something that,
I think if you do it,

00:14:14.211 --> 00:14:16.508
if you try to help other
people with their goals,

00:14:16.508 --> 00:14:17.492
it's always going to come back to you.

00:14:17.492 --> 00:14:20.845
It may not be in a way that you recognize,

00:14:20.845 --> 00:14:23.985
or that is immediate, but it comes back.

00:14:23.985 --> 00:14:26.966
Another quick example, on my
trip to LA, not too long ago,

00:14:26.966 --> 00:14:29.890
I took my TDS team to
see Tony Robbins in LA,

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:32.612
and I sit back an extra
day, to do meetings.

00:14:32.612 --> 00:14:34.119
I had a meeting with Brian Grazer,

00:14:34.119 --> 00:14:35.862
the legendary Hollywood producer.

00:14:35.862 --> 00:14:36.976
His assistant reached out to me,

00:14:36.976 --> 00:14:39.777
'cause Brian wanted to meet
with me, on one-on-one.

00:14:39.777 --> 00:14:42.145
I met with Lewis Howes,
later on that afternoon,

00:14:42.145 --> 00:14:43.326
from School of Greatness,

00:14:43.326 --> 00:14:44.892
and I was on his YouTube channel.

00:14:44.892 --> 00:14:45.725
We did an interview there.

00:14:45.725 --> 00:14:46.558
You guys can check it out.

00:14:46.558 --> 00:14:47.391
It's pretty fun.

00:14:47.391 --> 00:14:49.284
And I had other couple of
meetings, met with fans,

00:14:49.284 --> 00:14:50.945
and then I came back.

00:14:50.945 --> 00:14:52.594
Two weeks ago, I was watching
a video on Lewis's channel,

00:14:52.594 --> 00:14:53.886
with Wyclef Jean,

00:14:53.886 --> 00:14:56.850
and Wyclef, from the Fugees,
was talking about Brian Grazer,

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:59.221
and saying, "This guy
is one of the top guys,

00:14:59.221 --> 00:15:00.671
"in Hollywood history,

00:15:00.671 --> 00:15:02.597
"and someone who you need
to have on his show."

00:15:02.597 --> 00:15:03.430
And Lewis was saying,

00:15:03.430 --> 00:15:05.704
"Yeah, wow, that sounds
really interesting."

00:15:05.704 --> 00:15:08.362
I wrote to Lewis, and said, hey, Lewis,

00:15:08.362 --> 00:15:10.994
I saw Wyclef on your show,
he name dropped Brian Grazer.

00:15:10.994 --> 00:15:12.122
You looked interested.

00:15:12.122 --> 00:15:15.060
I actually met Brian a couple
hours before I met you,

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:15.970
when I was in LA.

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:17.234
I can set up the intro if you want,

00:15:17.234 --> 00:15:19.091
and see, maybe where that goes.

00:15:19.091 --> 00:15:20.263
And he said, "That would be amazing!

00:15:20.263 --> 00:15:21.347
"Thank you so much!"

00:15:21.347 --> 00:15:24.701
And so, I introduced Lewis
to Brian's assistant,

00:15:24.701 --> 00:15:27.233
and maybe something happens,
maybe something doesn't happen.

00:15:27.233 --> 00:15:28.742
Maybe it doesn't work out.

00:15:28.742 --> 00:15:30.794
Maybe they become mortal
enemies, who knows.

00:15:30.794 --> 00:15:32.331
But chances are, they're going to connect,

00:15:32.331 --> 00:15:33.569
something's going to work out,

00:15:33.569 --> 00:15:35.862
and both Lewis and Brian will be grateful

00:15:35.862 --> 00:15:38.317
that I was the one who
made that connection.

00:15:38.317 --> 00:15:39.368
Now, I'm not keeping scores.

00:15:39.368 --> 00:15:40.814
It's not like, hey, Lewis,

00:15:40.814 --> 00:15:43.544
I intro'd you to Brian,
so now you owe me this,

00:15:43.544 --> 00:15:45.332
for my book, or my whatever.

00:15:45.332 --> 00:15:46.291
That's not really how it works.

00:15:46.291 --> 00:15:48.092
It's not really about keeping scores.

00:15:48.092 --> 00:15:51.051
But, one, it just feels
good, to help people.

00:15:51.051 --> 00:15:53.978
And two, if you help
people, and it's consistent,

00:15:53.978 --> 00:15:55.778
then it comes back to you.

00:15:55.778 --> 00:15:56.804
It just always does.

00:15:56.804 --> 00:15:58.040
And so, when you're talking to people,

00:15:58.040 --> 00:15:59.467
understand what their main goals are.

00:15:59.467 --> 00:16:00.300
What are they trying to accomplish?

00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:01.262
What are their dreams?

00:16:01.262 --> 00:16:02.752
And to think, how can I help them?

00:16:02.752 --> 00:16:04.141
And maybe an introduction,

00:16:04.141 --> 00:16:08.832
and maybe just giving them a
push, beyond their limitations.

00:16:08.832 --> 00:16:09.890
It may just be believing in them.

00:16:09.890 --> 00:16:12.345
It may just be checking, and
seeing how they're doing.

00:16:12.345 --> 00:16:14.518
Finding ways to help them
accomplish their goal

00:16:14.518 --> 00:16:16.496
makes a huge, huge, huge difference.

00:16:16.496 --> 00:16:17.693
So, those are my seven ways

00:16:17.693 --> 00:16:19.398
on how to prove your people skills.

00:16:19.398 --> 00:16:22.698
I made this video, because
Amervim Bonano asked me to.

00:16:22.698 --> 00:16:23.913
So, if there's a topic
you'd like me to cover,

00:16:23.913 --> 00:16:25.481
in a future Seven Ways video,

00:16:25.481 --> 00:16:26.792
check out the link in the description,

00:16:26.792 --> 00:16:29.130
and go and cast your vote,
'til you're going to win,

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:31.210
and we'll see some content coming soon.

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:32.522
I'd love to know, what did
you think of this video?

00:16:32.522 --> 00:16:33.512
What was your favorite tip?

00:16:33.512 --> 00:16:35.241
What are you going to immediately apply,

00:16:35.241 --> 00:16:37.062
somehow to your life, or to your business?

00:16:37.062 --> 00:16:38.749
Is there any idea, that you
want to add to the list,

00:16:38.749 --> 00:16:39.642
that I missed?

00:16:39.642 --> 00:16:40.673
Leave it in the comments below.

00:16:40.673 --> 00:16:42.723
I'm really curious to see
what you guys have to say.

00:16:42.723 --> 00:16:45.041
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Dave Lukas,

00:16:45.041 --> 00:16:46.673
from the Misfit Entrepreneur.

00:16:46.673 --> 00:16:49.908
Dave, thank you so much
for being in this video,

00:16:49.908 --> 00:16:52.731
as well as posting the picture of my book,

00:16:52.731 --> 00:16:53.985
while you're on the beach.

00:16:53.985 --> 00:16:55.702
I really appreciate the support, man,

00:16:55.702 --> 00:16:57.960
and I'm so glad you enjoyed the read.

00:16:57.960 --> 00:16:59.387
So, thank you guys, so much for watching.

00:16:59.387 --> 00:17:00.678
I believe in you.

00:17:00.678 --> 00:17:02.421
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:17:02.421 --> 00:17:04.484
and whatever your one word is.

00:17:04.484 --> 00:17:05.455
Much love.

00:17:05.455 --> 00:17:06.872
I'll see ya soon.

